                  === WELCOME TO AETHERMUD ===

A roleplaying game set in the world of Rifts by Palladium Books. Earth,
hundreds of years in the future, after dimensional rifts tore reality
apart. Magic, technology, and aliens share a world that has not settled
down since.

WHERE YOU ARE
  You begin in the zone you chose during character creation:
    Americas   the edge of Chi-Town, the Coalition capital.
    Atlantis   the shores of Splynn and its Dimensional Market.
    Europe     New Camelot.
  Each start room describes its own surroundings. Type 'look' any time.

FIRST THINGS TO TRY
  look                  examine your surroundings.
  score                 your attributes, hit points, PPE and ISP.
  skills                what your OCC gave you.
  inventory / eq        what you carry, wear, and wield.
  help                  the help system. Type help, then a category
                        name, then a topic name.

STAYING ALIVE
  wield <weapon>        combat uses whatever you have wielded. A wielded
                        rifle is fired for you each round; there is no
                        separate firing command.
  wear <armor>          armor soaks damage before you do.
  kill <target>         start a fight. flee gets you out.
  rest                  recover. Inns and hostels have bunks.
  Watch what you attack. Many Rifts creatures are Mega-Damage and will
  ignore ordinary weapons while tearing through you.

WHO YOU ARE TALKING TO
  This game has no global chat channels. say, whisper, and ooc reach
  only your own room. To reach a player elsewhere you need telepathy
  (after being introduced) or a radio tuned to a shared frequency.
  introduce yourself to people you meet so they learn your name.
  tell reaches online staff only, not other players.

WHAT NOT TO LOSE
  Anything you have worn or wielded stays with you when you quit. Loose
  items in your pack are dropped on the floor where you log out. Equip
  what matters before you leave.

ROLEPLAY
  language              your languages. Races start with different ones.
  emote / pemote        act out something.
  position              set how you appear to be standing or sitting.
  Non-humans are not welcome everywhere. Coalition territory is openly
  hostile to D-Bees, and the right armor can change how strangers read
  you.

If something is broken, type bug <message>. Bad text is typo <message>.
Ideas are idea <message>.

The world outside your starting city is dangerous. Learn it slowly.
